  "notes": "Diff-derived. The fix at cd6e0ea940 changes the cohort store from holding trace IDs to holding full TraceSummary objects, so a selected trace survives a search that no longer returns it. Matches the issue's stated expectation, so no H2 divergence here. This entry DOES start from search results, twice, so it reuses the #4075 view-mode pin block verbatim (click the List radio after each search) rather than reauthoring it. The second search block drops its leading goto because the page is already loaded; re-navigating would reset the very state under test. Day 6: the view-mode pin steps were REMOVED for this pair. The List/Table Radio.Group and TraceTable do not exist at 2.18.0 at all; they arrive in 2.19.0. Waiting for [aria-label='Results view mode'] therefore timed out on the buggy side. This is a third instance of hazard H3 and it sharpens the rule: the mitigation for H3 is itself version-dependent, because you cannot pin a control that does not exist yet. Neither 2.18.0 (no toggle) nor 2.19.0 (defaults to List) renders a table here, so no pin is needed for this pair."
